    whatToFocusOn: 'Focus on Writs under Article 32 & 226, Kesavananda Bharati case (1973) Basic Structure Doctrine, FPTP vs Proportional Representation comparison, Governor discretionary powers under Article 163, and 73rd/74th Constitutional Amendment provisions.',
    whatToSkip: 'None—every chapter is foundational for Indian Polity.',
    seniorHinglishAdvice: 'Ye book Laxmikanth padhne se pehle padhna MANDATORY hai. Laxmikanth facts deti hai, but Indian Constitution at Work gives you the constitutional reasoning and philosophy required for GS2 Mains.',
    officialPdfUrl: 'https://ncert.nic.in/textbook.php?keps2=0-10',
